+Path cleaning rules let you normalize dynamic URLs into consistent patterns, reducing the cardinality of your path data. This makes your web analytics paths, entry paths, exit paths, outbound clicks, path breakdowns, and funnel breakdowns by event properties (such as `$pathname` or `$current_url`) more readable and actionable.
 
 For example, URLs like `/user/123`, `/user/456`, and `/user/789` can all be cleaned into `/user/:id` so they appear as a single row in your path tables.
 
